Current Si/SiGe heterostructure spin qubits utilize surface gates deposited directly on the quantum well. Baseline achieves T₂* ~ 20–30 µs. The primary decoherence mechanism is charge noise coupling via the interface disorder and remote ionized dopants.
**The 60-point ceiling of the old route has exhausted all degrees of freedom in gate geometry and doping concentration—further increasing the quantum well depth exacerbates strain relaxation, and further reducing the doping level increases series resistance beyond RF compatibility. Its limit is not technological, but physical: direct capacitive coupling between the gate and the electron gas creates a high-impedance pathway for charge fluctuations to modulate the Overhauser field and orbital levels.**

